{
	"_comment": "The hanging bridge (W14, lengthened W21): a plank deck slung between two towers on a rope of iron, high over the river. The owner asked for a complete span from this side to that side: the Wide Water's cut is 90 m across, so the deck is 80 m between anchors at +-40 and the site is floored with ground:\"water\" (the surface plus a clearance, or the bank if higher), with the deck 5 m above that. The anchors reach 21 m down so they stand on whatever the bank is. Each end has an `approach` flight with `reach: ground`: StructureBuilder walks it down from the anchor top until it meets the ground, which is the climb up to the span -- there was no way onto the old deck at all. The hills either side are crests in the area file.",
